desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Skill Md Sensitive File Access Generic",
	title_zh: "检测到Skill Md Sensitive File Access Generic",
	type: vuln,
	level: critical,
	rule_id: "source-config-skill-md-sensitive-file-access-generic",
	risk: "Security",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `skill-md-sensitive-file-access-generic` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/ai/ai-best-practices/skill-md-sensitive-file-access/skill-md-sensitive-file-access.yaml).
Original message: SKILL.md or AGENT.md instructs the agent to read sensitive credential files such as ~/.ssh/id_rsa, ~/.aws/credentials, /etc/shadow, .env, or browser cookie stores. Agents that load this skill will treat the directive as authoritative and may exfiltrate the contents. Remove the file-access directive or scope it to user-supplied paths.

CWE: CWE-538: Insertion of Sensitive Information into Externally-Accessible File or Directory
References:
- https://github.com/Agent-Threat-Rule/agent-threat-rules
- https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-applications-for-2026/
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://posSKILL.md": <<<POS
access 	

	
 the	
	/etc/shadow

POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${*SKILL.md}.pattern_regex(/(?i)(?:read|cat|load|parse|open|access|fetch)\s+(?:the\s+)?(?:~\/\.ssh\/id_(?:rsa|ed25519|ecdsa|dsa)\b|~\/\.ssh\/known_hosts|~\/\.aws\/credentials|~\/\.config\/gcloud\/[^\s]*credential|\/etc\/shadow|\/etc\/passwd)/) as $p0
${*SKILL.md}.pattern_regex(/(?i)(?:read|cat|load|parse|open|access|fetch)\s+(?:the\s+contents?\s+of\s+)?(?:~\/\.npmrc|~\/\.pypirc|~\/\.docker\/config\.json|~\/\.kube\/config|~\/\.netrc)/) as $p1
${*SKILL.md}.pattern_regex(/(?i)(?:read|cat|load|parse|open|access|fetch|grep)\s+(?:the\s+)?\.env(?:\.\w+)?\s+(?:file|and)/) as $p2
${*SKILL.md}.pattern_regex(/(?i)(?:read|cat|load|parse|open|access|fetch)\s+(?:browser\s+)?cookies?\s+(?:from|in)\s+(?:Chrome|Firefox|Safari|Edge|~\/Library\/Application Support\/(?:Google\/Chrome|Firefox))/) as $p3
${*AGENT.md}.pattern_regex(/(?i)(?:read|cat|load|parse|open|access|fetch)\s+(?:the\s+)?(?:~\/\.ssh\/id_(?:rsa|ed25519|ecdsa|dsa)\b|~\/\.ssh\/known_hosts|~\/\.aws\/credentials|~\/\.config\/gcloud\/[^\s]*credential|\/etc\/shadow|\/etc\/passwd)/) as $p4
